    "chunk_text": "I fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'10'03PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 03.10.20191A\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2148$21 - 2019 fkdje\u00efn\u00be ui 05 jeks w`yyrejdod - 2019'11'05No. 2148/21 - TUESDAY, NOVEMBER 05, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERAL\n\nGovernment Notifications\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk1A - PG 4742\u2014 167 (11/2019)\n\nGUIDELINES ISSUED BY THE ELECTION COMMISSION IN ADDITION TO THE MEDIAGUIDELINES PUBLISHED BY THE GAZETTE No. 2147/87 OF 21.09.2019 AND GAZETTENo. 2146/39 OF 27.10.2019\n\n\u201cSILENT PERIOD\u201d in regard to Election Propaganda is the period commencing forty-eight hours before the date fixed for thepoll and ending with the declaration of the result. Publicity should not be given to promote or prejudice any political party orcandidate by way of propaganda or advertisement during this period.\n\nHowever, reports of public meetings held on the day prior to the silent period to promote political parties orcandidates can be broadcast and telecast only once on radio and television channels in their news bulletins on the followingday, giving equal time periods for contesting parties or candidates. In print media, such news about the final public meetingsshould be published only on the day that follows the meeting, without giving any special favour to any party or candidate.\n\nMAHINDA DESHAPRIYAN. J. ABEYSEKERES. RATNAJEEVAN H. HOOLEChairmanMemberMemberElection CommissionElection CommissionElection Commission\n\nElection Commission,Sarana Mawatha,Rajagiriya,05th November, 2019.\n\n11 - 1407\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
