    "chunk_text": "\u201cUser Fee National Highways\u201d includes the Southern User Fee National Highway from Kottawa (0.000 km) to Pinnaduwa (95.275 km), Galle \u2013 Matara User Fee National Highway from Pinnaduwa (95.275km) to Godagama (124.806 km), Godagama \u2013 Kasagala Section of Southern Expressway User Fee National Highway from Godagama (124.806 km) to Kasagala (163.456 km), Colombo \u2013 Katunayake User Fee National Highway from Colombo (0.000km) to Katunayake (25.800km) and Outer Circular User fee National Highway from Kottawa (0.000 km) to Kerawalapitiya (28.867km)\n\n(b) a second or subsequent offence; to a fine not exceeding fifty thousand rupees. 11. The National Thoroughfares (User Fee) Regulations No. 2 of 2015 published in the Gazette Extraordinary No. 1924/8 of July, 20, 2015, Gazette Extraordinary No. 1924/52 of July, 25, 2015 and the National Thoroughfares (User Fee) Regulations No. 1 of 2015 published in the Gazette Extraordinary No. 1912/2 of April, 27, 2015 are hereby rescinded without prejudice to anything done thereunder.\n\n12. The Regulations relevant to Electronic Toll Collection System (ETC) is included in the Annex 1.\n\n4AI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'08Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 08.11.2019\n\nAnnex 1\n\n(1) (1) An owner or driver of a vehicle who is desirous of making payments electronically (hereinafter referred as \u201cE-tag user\u201d) shall register with the Road Development Authority, established under the Road Development Authority Act, No. 73 of 1981, (hereinafter referred to as \u201cthe Authority\u201d) and shall be required to open an Electronic Toll Collection System User Fee Account (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cETCS Account\u201d) at the Customer Service Centre of the Authority.\n\n(2) Every application for registration as an E- tag user shall be made to the Customer Service Centre of the Authority."
