    "chunk_text": "(1) (1) An owner or driver of a vehicle who is desirous of making payments electronically (hereinafter referred as \u201cE-tag user\u201d) shall register with the Road Development Authority, established under the Road Development Authority Act, No. 73 of 1981, (hereinafter referred to as \u201cthe Authority\u201d) and shall be required to open an Electronic Toll Collection System User Fee Account (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cETCS Account\u201d) at the Customer Service Centre of the Authority.\n\n(2) Every application for registration as an E- tag user shall be made to the Customer Service Centre of the Authority.\n\n(4) Every E-tag user shall enter into an Electronic Toll Collection System User Fee customer agreement (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cETCS customer agreement\u201d) subject to the terms and conditions specified in such agreement.\n\n(5) Every E-tag issued shall be fitted on to the windscreen or head lamp of the vehicle.\n\n(6) It shall be the duty of every E-tag user to maintain a sufficient credit balance in the ETCS Account at all times when using an Electronic user fee collection lane (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cETC lane\u201d) enabling such person to make the payment of such user fee.\n\n(7) In case of insufficient credit, the E- tag user may top-up the ETCS account and the processing time of such top-up shall be not less than one hour before the E-Tag user may be able to use ETC lane.\n\n(8) Every E-tag user shall ensure that the E- tag is in proper working order and shall inform the Authority of any damage or loss to such E- tag.\n\n(2) (1) where an E-tag user with sufficient credit to pay the user fee, enters the User Fee National Highway from an interchange other than from a designated location, such E-tag user shall be permitted to proceed along the ETC lane of such interchange.\n\n(2) Where a vehicle fitted with an E- tag is being used on an ETC lane, the user fee shall be debited against the ETCS"
