    "md5": "71e2cde6d0d537727c2424879e65df4c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1876,
    "chunk_text": "(2) Where the driver is unable to surrender the ticket to the Teller, and the Teller fails to identify the entry location, the driver shall be deemed to have travelled the entire distance of the User Fee National Highway from the furthest possible point of entry to the actual point of exit and shall accordingly be charged a fee at the rates speci\ufb01 ed in Part A of the schedule to these regulations.\n\n(2) The gates so positioned along the User Fee National Highway shall be owned, operated and maintained by the Authority, and each gate shall be manned by a Teller.\n\n(3) The Teller shall be responsible for the collection of the user fee at every gate referred to in paragraph (2), in such sum as is speci\ufb01 ed in Part A of the Schedule to these regulations from every driver using such User Fee National Highways :\n\nProvided that the provisions of these regulations shall not apply to a driver who is driving a vehicle of a category speci\ufb01 ed in Part B of the Schedule to these regulations, which is exempt from such payment.\n\n(7) The Teller shall at such times as are speci\ufb01 ed, hand over the day\u2019s collection of the fees to the of\ufb01 cer authorized in that behalf by the Authority and obtain a receipt in respect of such amount.\n\n(8) The money so collected as user fee shall be credited to the Fund of the Authority and be used for the purpose of developing and maintaining the User Fee National Highways to which these regulations apply.\n\n(9) For the purpose of these regulations-\n\n\u201cTeller\u201d means an of\ufb01 cer who is manning the gates at an interchange;\n\n\u201cUser Fee National Highways\u201d includes Barawakumbuka \u2013 Mattala User Fee National Highway (Section of Extension of Southern Expressway) from Barawakumbuka (178.656 km) to Mattala (200.451 km) and Andarawewa \u2013 Hambantota User Fee National Highway from Andarawewa (0.000km) to Hambantota (16.558km)."
