    "chunk_text": "And whereas Madhu pilgrimage regulations have been promulgated by Gazette Notification No. 185 dated 19thMarch 1982 under Pilgrimages Ordinance No. 13 of 1896 with the view of providing the opportunity for the hundreds ofthousand of people visiting the Madhu Pilgrims' area during the said Madhu Pilgrims' season to stay in without their havingto undergo difficulties.\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nSeal\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk1A- G 31455 \u2014 27 (11/2019)\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'13PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 13.11.20192A\n\nI do by virtue of the powers vested in me by Article 32(2)(h) of the Constitution of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka proclaim the extent of land set out in the first schedule as an area of veneration for the religious well-being of the hundreds of thousand of Catholic devotees who visit to pay homage at the Holy Shrine of our Lady of Madhu.\n\nGiven at Colombo, on this 11th day of November Two Thousand and Nineteen.\n\nBy Order of His Excellency,\n\nUDAYA R. SENEVIRATNE,Secretary to the President.\n\nSchedule 01\n\nThe allotment of land of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka situated in the village of Madhu in theGrama Niladhari's Division of Madhu in the Divisional Secretary's Division of Madhu in the District of Mannar in theNorthern Province and depicted as Lots Nos. A, B, C, D, E and F in the Tracing No. Ma/MDU/2018/185 prepared by theSurveyor General.\n\n11 - 1607\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
