    "chunk_text": "wxl 2149$22- 2019 fkdje\u00efn\u00be ui 14 jeks n%yiam;skaod - 2019'11'14No. 2149/22 \u2013 THURSDAY, NOVEMBER 14, 2019\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART I: SECTION (I) - GENERAL\n\nGovernment Notifications\n\nYS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www. documents.gov.lk\n\n1A - G 031459 - 12 (2019/11)\n\nPilgrimages Ordinance\n\nREGULATIONS made by the Minister of Internal & Home Affairs and Provincial Councils & Local Government in termsof section 2 of Pilgrimages Ordinance. (Chap. 175).\n\nWAJIRA ABEYWARDHANA,Internal & Home Affairs andProvincial Councils & LocalGovernment.\n\nMinistry of Internal & Home Affairs and Provincial Councils& Local Government, Nila Medura Building,Elvitigala Mawatha,Narahenpita,Colombo 05,04th October, 2019.\n\nRegulations\n\n1. These regulations may be cited as the regulation of Baddegama Perahera Festival of Gothatuwa SripadaChaithyarama Temple, in the Grama Niladaris\u2019s Division of No. 198, Ganegama North, Divisional Secretary\u2019sDivision of Baddegama, Galle District.2. In these regulations\n\nI fldgi : f\u00feoh - Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'14PART I : SECTION I - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 14.11.20192A\n\n\u201cCamp area\u201d means the area described in the schedule.\u201cDistrict Secretary/ Government Agent\u201d means the Government Agent of Galle Administrative District and italso includes any officer authorized by him in terms of regulation 4.\u201cMedical Officer\u201d means the Medical officer of health in charge of the camp area.\u201cPilgrim\u201d means any person who enters and stays within the camp area for any purpose.\u201cPolice Officer\u201d includes any Grama Niladhari in charge of the camp area.\u201cPublic Health Inspector\u201d means the public health inspector in charge of the camp area."
