    "chunk_text": "1AIII fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'02'25PART III \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 25.02.2019\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%hThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nw;s \u00fafYI EXTRAORDINARY\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Redemption Notices\n\nwxl 2150$8 \u2013 2019 fkdje\u00efn\u00be 19 jeks w\u00d5yrejdod \u2013 2019'11'19No. 2150/8 \u2013 TUESDAY, NOVEMBER 19, 2019\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nREVOCATION UNDER SECTION 39(1)\n\nThe land specified morefully in the Order No. 172 of 2018 dated02.08.2018 made under the Proviso (a) to Section 38 of the LandAcquisition Act (Chapter 460) and published in the GazetteExtra Ordinary No. 2082/61 dated 03.08.2018 was vested in theDemocratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka. But the possession ofthe land described below has not yet been taken for and on behalf ofthe Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka. Therefore, I, GayanthaKarunatilleke, Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms, byvirtue of powers vested in me under Section 39 (1) of the LandAcquisition Act, do hereby revoke the Order made in respect of thelands sepcified morefully in the Schedule below, under the aforesaidvesting Order No. 172 of 2018 dated 02.08.2018 published in theGazette Extra Ordinary No. 2082/61 dated 03.08.2018.\n\nGayantha Karunatilleke,Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms.\n\nMy Ref. No.: 4-3/7/2018/HW/65.Divisional Secretary\u2019s No.: \u00f3\u00df$m%d'f,a'$b$3$2018'Ministry of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms,\u201cMihikatha Medura\u201d,Rajamalwatta Road,Battaramulla.08th November, 2019.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nAllotments of land total extent of about 0.9149 Hectare, depicted\n\nin below names and extents as Lot \u2018A\u2019 and \u2018B\u2019 in the Advance Tracing\n\nNo. GA/MEE/2018/193 dated 04.06.2018 prepared by the Senior\n\nSuperintendent of Surveys of Gampaha District, situated in the\n\nVillage called Galgamuwa in the Grama Niladhari Division No. 338"
